# DevOps Connection

File I/O is a basic but important Linux skill used regularly in DevOps.

Common examples include:

```text
Configuration files
       ↓
/etc/*.conf

Application logs
       ↓
/var/log/*

Scripts
       ↓
*.sh

Environment/configuration data
       ↓
*.env / config files
```

For example, during troubleshooting:

```bash
tail -n 50 application.log
```

can quickly show recent application activity, while:

```bash
grep "ERROR" application.log
```

can help identify errors.

